-- Assign spiral to existing entities (ex29). Twin of 057-spiral-assign.bqn.
-- Formal witness: the five derived positions align on the Coin query and scatter back through its entity lineage.
-- Five coins already in the world rearrange onto the spiral: no spawning here, the same polar formula writes positions to an existing selection, and index counts within the selection, not the world.
-- One world: the demo's 8 entities plus row 8, the Player anchor (pos 100 200, not a Coin) — the .bqn's external playerPos folded into the entity world, expected values remapped over 9 rows.
-- index is the position within the selection, not the world row id. Coin rows 0 2 3 5 7 take spiral indices 0..4; non-coin rows and the Player remain unchanged.
-- Steel pins the current CBQN values; the BQN twin checks them within 1e-9 and keeps the zip-shape counterexample.
--! registry ../registries/057-spiral-assign.reg
--! expect coin = 1 0 1 1 0 1 0 1 0
--! expect pos = 100 200 10 10 99.26272266318988 200.67559020761567 100.17431148549531 198.00761060381652 20 20 101.82628428702617 202.3800600208737 30 30 96.06076898795116 199.3054072893323 100 200
--! expect-n 9

Coin , pos = Player.pos + polar(index, index * 137.5)
